{#-
  Template for the generated schema diagram page (docs/schema_diagram.md).

  Every name and definition here comes from the LinkML schema via
  scripts/gen_schema_diagram.py. The only prose written by hand is `intro`,
  which lives in diagram-layout.yaml.

  `box` renders one node of the diagram and calls itself for the nodes inside
  it. Cards (classes with nothing nested in them) and levels (classes that
  contain others) go in separate rows: letting them share one flow puts a lone
  card beside a whole nested level, which reads as an accident rather than a
  structure.
-#}
{%- macro box(node) -%}
{% if node.children %}
<div class="zapp-box zapp-box--d{{ node.tint }}">
<span class="zapp-box__title"><a class="zapp-box__link" href="#{{ node.anchor }}" title="{{ node.description|e }}">{{ node.label|e }}</a></span>
{% if node.cards %}
<div class="zapp-box__cards">
{% for child in node.cards %}
{{ box(child) }}
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}
{% if node.levels %}
<div class="zapp-box__levels">
{% for child in node.levels %}
{{ box(child) }}
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}
</div>
{%- else %}
<a class="zapp-leaf" href="#{{ node.anchor }}" title="{{ node.description|e }}">{{ node.label|e }}</a>
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro reference(class_name) -%}
[Full schema reference for {{ class_name }} →](../{{ class_name }}/)
{%- endmacro -%}

# Schema Diagram

{{ intro }}

{# The diagram gets a heading of its own so the table of contents has something
   to point at, and so it sits level with the sections below it. -#}
